# Do NOT set merge=union on tools/step0_empty_assets.csv.
#
# In that file a row's PRESENCE is a state flag, so a union merge is wrong twice
# over: it resurrects a row that one side deliberately deleted (a date rerun.py
# just finished processing gets re-queued forever), and it silently keeps two
# rows for the same date when both sides wrote a different remark.
#
# Union merge was originally added to stop the CI push step hitting conflicts on
# this file. That is no longer needed: the real cause was rerun.py reordering
# every row on each run, which sort_index() in process_empty_asset_list() fixed.
# Genuine conflicts are now rare and the push retry loop in run_rerun.yml reports
# them instead of resolving them wrongly.
